+## On your watch (Wear OS, Android app)
+
+With your position showing, a paired Wear OS watch (Wear OS 3 or later, such as a Pixel Watch) shows the one thing a glance needs: **where next, and when**. It shows the next waypoint and how far along the route it is (*3/7*), its magnetic bearing and distance, the ETE at your actual ground speed and the ETA in Zulu, time on this leg, ground speed, and altitude beside the leg's planned altitude. The figures come from the phone, the same as the map and the alerts; the watch only counts the clock. Off the route it says **Off route**. A picture older than 10 seconds greys and says its age, and after a minute without the phone it says **No data from phone**, so a frozen number never reads as current.
+
+It is the NavAid watch app, with a screen, a tile (swipe from the watch face) and a complication for any watch face (the ETE under the waypoint). Its APK is attached to the Android release beside the phone's, and installed over Wi-Fi debugging; the steps are in `mobile/README.md`. The in-flight alerts already reach the watch without it, as notifications. Gist: `featureWear` (on), `wearSendSec` (2 s), `wearStaleSec` (10 s).
+
